</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Account and session information</th><td data-label="How it is used and where it is handled">Account identifiers such as your DID, handle and provider address; OAuth authorization state; upstream session credentials; and the Nest session binding support sign-in, authenticated actions and access revocation. Nest holds the normal upstream session credentials.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Account actions and content</th><td data-label="How it is used and where it is handled">Posts, messages, media, searches, reactions, profile changes and other requested actions pass through the services needed to perform them. Nest processes the content it relays; direct recipients receive their own requests.</td></tr>
